  "reason": "The current best is config_024 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) at 0.629 acc, and all multimodal experiments so far have used concat fusion. The only untested fusion strategy is weighted, which directly tests whether the modality combination mechanism matters beyond simple concatenation. This is a clean single-variable change from the current best, so any performance shift can be cleanly attributed to fusion strategy. Given the limited budget, exploiting the strongest known direction (multiprofile + vit_l + avgpool) while resolving the fusion question is more informative than introducing an untested RNA encoder (scvi/scgpt) whose standalone performance is unknown. If weighted fusion improves on concat, we gain a better configuration immediately; if not, we confirm concat is sufficient and can redirect effort to RNA encoder choice."
